+    "But the conservative analyst is right that the entry point is stretched, and stretched entries have a cost even when the trend is intact.",
+    "But the stock at $615 is priced for a forward EPS estimate of $15.57 that requires core earnings to roughly triple, off a base where 20% of the most recent quarter's net income came from a non-operating investment gain and where operating cash flow was flattered by a $2.36B one-time payables spike.",
+    "Category: Company; Item: $1T market cap; Detail: AMD crossed $1T for first time on 2026-09-21; 4th US chipmaker; Direction / Implication for AMD: Bullish milestone; raises valuation-risk profile",
